{"title":"Career Roadmap · Critical Care Technician","role":"Critical Care Technician","summary":"A Critical Care Technician supports the multidisciplinary intensive-care team in caring for critically ill patients. The role combines critical-care equipment management, patient monitoring, infection control, emergency preparedness, specimen handling, basic clinical support, and ICU operations.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Anaesthesia & Operation Theatre Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Critical Care Technician supports the multidisciplinary intensive-care team in caring for critically ill patients. The role combines critical-care equipment management, patient monitoring, infection control, emergency preparedness, specimen handling, basic clinical support, and ICU operations."},{"type":"p","text":"For a graduate from Anaesthesia & Operation Theatre Technology, the strongest pathway is to build on existing knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia equipment"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Operating-room procedures"},{"text":"Sterile technique"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Critical-care equipment"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Critical Care Technicians generally work under the direction and scope defined by the healthcare institution and applicable professional requirements. They support, but do not replace, physicians, nurses, respiratory therapists, or other licensed professionals."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc / Degree in Anaesthesia & OT Technology","Clinical Internship","OT + Anaesthesia + ICU Exposure","Critical Care Technician","Experienced ICU / Critical Care Technician","Senior Critical Care Technician","ICU Technician / Critical Care Coordinator","Critical Care Operations / Technical Supervisor"]},{"type":"p","text":"Additional critical-care training and supervised ICU experience are highly valuable."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG Years 1–2"},{"text":"Anatomy, physiology, pharmacology and OT foundations"}],[{"text":"UG Years 3–4"},{"text":"Anaesthesia, patient monitoring and critical-care principles"}],[{"text":"Clinical Internship"},{"text":"ICU, OT and emergency-care exposure"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Equipment, monitoring and bedside support"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Advanced critical-care procedures and emergency response"}],[{"text":"Senior Career"},{"text":"Technical supervision, equipment and ICU operations"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Healthcare Foundations"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic Focus"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Physiology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Pharmacology fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Basic patient care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respiratory system"},{"text":"Cardiovascular system"},{"text":"Nervous system"},{"text":"Renal system"},{"text":"Fluid and electrolyte balance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Vital signs"},{"text":"Basic documentation"},{"text":"Safe patient transfer"},{"text":"Healthcare communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Anaesthesia & OT Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia techniques"},{"text":"Airway management"},{"text":"Anaesthesia machines"},{"text":"Surgical procedures"},{"text":"OT equipment"},{"text":"Sterilization"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Basic pharmacology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment Familiarity"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Anaesthesia workstation"},{"text":"Ventilator"},{"text":"Multiparameter monitor"},{"text":"Pulse oximeter"},{"text":"Capnography"},{"text":"Suction systems"},{"text":"Infusion pumps"},{"text":"Defibrillator"},{"text":"Oxygen delivery systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Critical Care Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the key transition toward critical-care practice."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Intensive care principles"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation"},{"text":"Hemodynamic monitoring"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"ABG fundamentals"},{"text":"Fluid and electrolyte management"},{"text":"Shock"},{"text":"Sepsis"},{"text":"Acute respiratory failure"},{"text":"Renal failure"},{"text":"Neurological emergencies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the clinical significance of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Heart rate"},{"text":"Blood pressure"},{"text":"SpO₂"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"Temperature"},{"text":"ECG"},{"text":"Capnography"},{"text":"Urine output"},{"text":"Basic invasive monitoring concepts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician's role is to accurately monitor, support equipment, identify abnormal changes and promptly escalate concerns to the responsible clinical team."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Advanced Critical-Care Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on integrating:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ICU workflow"},{"text":"Ventilator support"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Patient transport"},{"text":"Equipment preparation"},{"text":"Critical-care documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"ICU Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Admission","Initial Assessment","Monitoring Setup","Airway / Respiratory Support","Hemodynamic Monitoring","Treatment Support","Continuous Observation","Clinical Escalation","Documentation","Transfer / Discharge"]}]},{"heading":"Critical Care Equipment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong technician should understand the purpose, operation and basic troubleshooting of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Respiratory Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanical ventilators"},{"text":"Oxygen systems"},{"text":"Suction apparatus"},{"text":"Nebulizers"},{"text":"Airway equipment"},{"text":"Bag-valve masks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ECG monitors"},{"text":"Pulse oximeters"},{"text":"Non-invasive BP monitors"},{"text":"Invasive pressure-monitoring systems"},{"text":"Capnography"},{"text":"Temperature monitoring"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Defibrillators"},{"text":"Crash carts"},{"text":"Bag-valve masks"},{"text":"Emergency airway equipment"},{"text":"Suction systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Infusion Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Syringe pumps"},{"text":"Infusion pumps"},{"text":"Fluid warmers where applicable"}]}]},{"heading":"Airway & Respiratory Support","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airway anatomy"},{"text":"Oxygen delivery systems"},{"text":"Basic airway adjuncts"},{"text":"Bag-mask ventilation"},{"text":"Endotracheal tube fundamentals"},{"text":"Tracheostomy care principles"},{"text":"Mechanical ventilation concepts"},{"text":"Ventilator alarms"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ventilator Concepts"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Tidal volume"},{"text":"Respiratory rate"},{"text":"FiO₂"},{"text":"PEEP"},{"text":"Pressure vs volume modes"},{"text":"Peak pressure"},{"text":"Plateau pressure"},{"text":"Oxygenation vs ventilation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A technician should not independently alter ventilator settings unless 