xt":"Hand hygiene"},{"text":"PPE"},{"text":"Aseptic technique"},{"text":"Sterile procedures"},{"text":"Catheter-care principles"},{"text":"Ventilator-associated infection prevention"},{"text":"Biomedical waste management"},{"text":"Environmental cleaning"},{"text":"Isolation precautions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Major Principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Hand Hygiene"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Aseptic Technique"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Equipment Cleaning"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Appropriate PPE"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Isolation Procedures"},{"type":"p","text":"="},{"type":"p","text":"Reduced Healthcare-Associated Infection Risk"}]},{"heading":"Medication & Infusion Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The technician should understand the purpose and risks associated with common ICU medication categories, while medication preparation/administration remains subject to professional scope and institutional policy."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the basics of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sedatives"},{"text":"Analgesics"},{"text":"Vasopressors"},{"text":"Inotropes"},{"text":"Antibiotics"},{"text":"Anticoagulants"},{"text":"Electrolyte replacement"},{"text":"Emergency medications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is to understand equipment, monitoring and safety implications, not to independently prescribe or administer medications outside authorized scope."}]},{"heading":"Patient Transport","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Critical-care transport is a major practical competency."},{"type":"p","text":"Before transport, check:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Oxygen supply"},{"text":"Battery status"},{"text":"Monitor"},{"text":"Ventilator where applicable"},{"text":"Emergency equipment"},{"text":"Infusion pumps"},{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Required documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Transport Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Patient Asse